      },
      "gate": "The val gate re-scores the staged winner on a split nothing in the loop has fitted, per category. It fails when the val mean falls, or when any category with enough support drops by more than its tolerance; a category already perfect has no tolerance at all. A failed gate discards the candidate. The report does not record its generation, so a generation is shown only when the same trace was later reviewed or adopted.",
      "live": "Containers running the rollout image, the supervisor loop if it is up, and the tail of the supervisor's log. The generation number is read from that log.",
      "promotions": "The reward curve: each adopted winner's macro-F1 on train, with its held-out macro-F1 on val. A generation appears here only if promote found an eligible candidate, the gate passed it and, when review is on, the reviewer did not refuse it. The dashed line is the train baseline the first winner beat.",
      "reviews": "A stronger model asked, after the gate passes, whether the candidate earned its score. Veto only: it can refuse an adoption, never cause one, and never changes a reward. A refusal counts only when it cites a rubric concern and quotes the diff's changed lines; anything else is recorded and passes, with the reason shown. Too many refusals in a row stop the run, marked here as run stopped.",
      "rollouts": {
        "terms": [
          [
            "scored",
            "the host measured the returned table"
          ],
          [
            "artifact_unchanged",
            "no table came back to score: the rollout never reached finalize"
          ],
          [
            "guard_rejected",
            "the table reached outside the text it was handed (imports, open, eval, dunders)"
